{
  "case_id": "2001-01-631",
  "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Thompson, isn't it so that in Bostick the police did inform the passengers that they had a right to refuse consent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Larry D. Thompson, Esq.",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For example, the Eleventh Circuit noted the importance of Officer Hoover at the front of the bus and pointed out that his presence might lead a -- a passenger to believe that he or she could not leave the bus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Thompson, did they know that he was an officer? Was it clear that he was an officer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, I assume the other policy objection is, the underlying premise of Justice Breyer's suggestion is the Government has some obligation to teach everybody about their rights. And that's a -- that's a sweeping proposition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Didn't they make it clear that they were asking permission which suggests that the person has the ability to deny permission?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would like to address the Government's argument that there is a per se rule in this case. And one of the points they make is -- in their reply brief at 4, they argue that because we have not identified one case in which the Eleventh Circuit has ruled in favor of the Government in an on-bus case -- I have been able to identify three unpublished decisions, which I'd like to cite to the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9d20fdc73c8a8f73c9364cdfbd0df79f268f7976ab997f73818e5702a3202ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9d20fdc73c8a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
